{"id":9434,"date":"2023-07-11T19:46:35","date_gmt":"2023-07-12T02:46:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=9434"},"modified":"2025-02-25T17:42:00","modified_gmt":"2025-02-26T01:42:00","slug":"0-7-propellers-and-motors","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-7-propellers-and-motors\/","title":{"rendered":"0.7: Troubleshooting, Repair, and Maintenance"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221300e2057\" name=\"6a221300e2057\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is Troubleshooting?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \">\n<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n<p>Troubleshooting is the process of finding out the cause of a problem through a series of testing various guesses. You probably troubleshoot every day without knowing it! Think of all the steps you take when your TV remote, computer, cell phone, or other appliance stop working. You might turn it off and on again, test new batteries, or find out something was stuck. Similarly, you may need to troubleshoot your drone from time to time.<\/p>\n<p>For CoDrone EDU, you can prevent most issues by following the pre-flight checklist you learned about in a previous lesson.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9598&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221300e2190\" name=\"6a221300e2190\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Propeller Replacement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 11\">\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\n<div class=\"column\">\n<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \">\n<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 11\">\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\n<div class=\"column\">\n<p>Propellers can be removed to clear out debris from under the propeller hub. A propeller should be replaced if it\u2019s bent, chipped, or cracked, and it begins affecting the drone\u2019s flight. Use the included propeller removal tool to remove the propeller.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9440&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 11\">\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\n<div class=\"column\">\n<p>Insert the fork-shaped end of the tool under the propeller hub, then push the handle down, like a lever. Then, grab your new propeller. Remember to match the same propeller orientation with your new propeller. The best way to check is to match the letter on the bottom of the propeller.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9628&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \">\n<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n<p>The new propeller can be pushed onto the shaft of the motor. Be sure it\u2019s fully inserted, so it doesn\u2019t detach during flight. Make sure that the replacement propeller\u2019s rotation is correct, and perform a quick flight check.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9439&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/pKWpuLhehHU&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Video Tutorial&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221300e2214\" name=\"6a221300e2214\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Motor Replacement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \">\n<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n<p>If the propeller is in good condition, but you are experiencing drift or a motor not spinning, you may need to replace the motor. Use this visual guide to inspect your motors. A damaged motor may cause damage to the drone when taking off.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9936&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Before replacing a motor, remember there are <b>2 types of motors<\/b>, denoted by the color of the wires. Motor direction needs to match propeller directions.<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Blue\/red is clockwise (cw)<\/li>\n<li>Black\/white is counterclockwise (ccw)<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9441&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \">\n<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n<p>Take note of which motor is in which position. You will need to remember this when you replace the motor. Always replace a motor with the same color wires.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9630&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/-uVii37aEYY&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Video Tutorial&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221300e22de\" name=\"6a221300e22de\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>More Troubleshooting<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element \">\n<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n<p>There are many other common issues that you may encounter while using CoDrone EDU. Before frantically alerting your classmates, teacher, or coach, always ask yourself if you\u2019ve followed all the basic checks you\u2019ve learned about so far.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Are my batteries fully charged?<\/li>\n<li>Am I aiming the antenna at the drone?<\/li>\n<li>Is my controller in the right state for piloting?<\/li>\n<li>What speed am I on?<\/li>\n<li>Did I pair correctly?<\/li>\n<li>Did I remember to clean my propellers and check my motors?<\/li>\n<li>Should I replace anything?<\/li>\n<li>Did I trim my drone?<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Challenge yourself to come up with your own troubleshooting checklist and flow chart that you can follow. With practice, you will become in expert in troubleshooting your drone and controller.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221300e2342\" name=\"6a221300e2342\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Helpdocs<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Since there are many more questions that may come up, we have put together a list of questions and answers for you to help debug any issues that come up along the way. If there\u2019s a question that you can\u2019t answer, visit our\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/robolink.helpdocs.io\/\">Helpdocs<\/a>\u00a0page with all of our Frequently Asked Questions. If you\u2019re still stuck, ask a parent, teacher, or coach to email us![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9937&#8243; img_size=&#8221;470&#215;394&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221300e2399\" name=\"6a221300e2399\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Course Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Congratulations!<\/p>\n<p>You have completed the Getting Started Course. Always review this course if you need help with basic onboarding steps or need a refresher. To get started with programming, pick one of the two following courses.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/course\/blockly-with-codrone-edu\/\">Blockly Programming Course<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/course\/python-with-codrone-edu\/\">Python Programming Course<\/a>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 What is Troubleshooting? [vc_column_text] Troubleshooting is the process of finding out the cause of a problem through a series of testing various guesses. You probably troubleshoot every&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/0-7-propellers-and-motors\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":9813,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":9219,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[4328,2179,8471,8467,8488,8469,2105],"class_list":["post-9434","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-maintenance","lesson-tag-repair","lesson-tag-replacement","lesson-tag-storage","lesson-tag-testing","lesson-tag-troubleshooting","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/9434","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":29,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/9434\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13471,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/9434\/revisions\/